        "note_tweet": {
          "entities": {},
          "text": "明天，中国的高考就要开始了。\n对于许多人来说，这或许是准备了很久、也等待了很久的一天。那些写满笔记的课本、一次又一次修改的错题、熬夜学习的夜晚，还有面对未来时的不安与期待，都会在明天化作迈向前方的脚步。\n我知道，考试来临的时候，难免会感到紧张。担心自己是否准备充分，担心结果会不会辜负一直以来的努力。\n但是，请不要忘记，能够走到这里，本身就已经是一件值得肯定的事情。\n无论过去的成绩如何，无论此刻的心情怎样，希望你能够相信自己曾经付出的每一分努力。试着像平时练习时那样，认真地完成眼前的每一道题目，然后把答案交给未来。\n愿你们合上笔盖的时候，能够为自己的坚持感到骄傲。\n祝所有参加高考的同学考试顺利，得偿所愿。\n\nTomorrow marks the beginning of the National College Entrance Examination in China.\nFor many students, this is a day they’ve been preparing for and waiting for over a long period of time. The textbooks filled with notes, the countless practice papers, the late nights spent studying, and the mix of hope and uncertainty about the future have all led to this moment.\nIt’s natural to feel nervous before an important exam. You may wonder whether you’ve prepared enough, or whether the results will reflect all the effort you’ve put in.\nBut please remember this: making it this far is already something to be proud of.\nNo matter what your past scores were, and no matter how you’re feeling right now, I hope you can trust in the work you’ve done. Take each question one at a time, just as you have during your preparation, and leave the rest to the future.\nWhen you put down your pen at the end of the exam, I hope you’ll be able to look back on your efforts with pride.\nWishing every student taking the Gaokao the very best of luck. May your hard work be rewarded."
        },
